  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner who became well-known for completing marathons while wearing a bionic suit despite being paralysed from the chest down, has passed away following an accident in Jordan on 22 August. Lomas was originally paralysed in 2007 after being thrown from her horse during the Osberton Horse Trials in Nottinghamshire, suffering severe injuries including a broken neck and back. She went on to raise nearly £1 million for charity through various events, most notably completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days and the 2016 Great North Run while pregnant, both times using her bionic suit. She was also honored by lighting the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square in 2012. Her family has asked for privacy during their time of grief."
